                <head>Agreements between the Rubber Reserve Company and the colonial Governments of
                    Trinidad, British Guiana, and British Honduras for the purchase of exportable
                    rubber</head>
                <p>[Agreement with Trinidad was signed on August 5, 1942, by the Colonial Secretary
                    and the Rubber Reserve Company, an agency of the United States Government. The
                    agreements with British Guiana and British Honduras were signed on August 10,
                    1942, by their respective Governors and the Rubber Reserve Company. The texts of
                    these agreements are not printed. They were of the same general nature as
                    agreements made with a number of American Republics.]</p>
            </div>
